<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sayn Abbey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1202</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sayn Abbey is a former Premonstratensian monastery in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bendorf">Bendorf</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koblenz">Koblenz</a>, founded in 1202 by Count Henry II of Sayn. It served as the burial place of the counts of Sayn, and its church keeps a medieval arm reliquary of the apostle Simon. It was dissolved in 1803, and the church is now a parish church.</p></div>
